// Naevius, a Roman wine trader settled among the Aedui at Noviodunum. Trades,
// and knows everyone's business.
=== start
[flag naevius_met] -> again
~ set naevius_met
A low room stacked with amphorae, a brazier, and a Roman in a wine-colored tunic who says "Welcome, welcome" in Gallic with an Aeduan accent, and then, seeing your cloak, "Cadurci! Long way. You'll want a drink. Everyone who comes this far wants a drink."
-> hub

=== again
"Back! Drink?"
-> hub

=== hub
* "Show me what you've got." -> trade
* "What's the news?" -> news
* "Tell me about the depot." -> depot
* [!flag naevius_orbius] "What's the quartermaster like?" -> orbius
* "Goodbye." -> END

=== trade
~ barter
"Italian red, Aeduan bread, Roman bandages. Everything a war needs."
-> hub

=== news
[!flag cenabum_burned] "News? Cenabum, still. They're still killing Romans in Cenabum, or they were. And Caesar's coming back over the mountains, and the Arvernian boy calls himself king." He pours. "I've lived here twenty years. I married an Aeduan woman. I'm waiting to find out which side I'm on."
[flag cenabum_burned, flag cenabum_saved] "Cenabum's burned. But they got out, they say, by daylight, the old man sent them out before Caesar came. Caesar found an empty town." He pours, and drinks it himself. "I knew people there. I'd like to think some of them are drinking somewhere tonight."
[flag cenabum_burned, !flag cenabum_saved] "Cenabum's gone." He doesn't pour, for once. "Caesar took it at night. They tried to get out over the bridge, all of them at once. I knew people there."
[flag aedui_wavering] "And the young men up the hill are talking about the Arverni a great deal more than they used to. When the Aedui go, they'll come for us first, the Romans in the town. I have a boat."
-> hub

=== depot
"Caesar's money box." He laughs. "I sell them wine. The quartermaster pays on time, which is more than any Gaul ever did. The Aeduan at the gate takes a little, the watch takes a little, everyone takes a little, the Romans pretend not to see, and the wine goes in." He winks. "So do other things. Ask Dagolitos. Ask him nicely, with silver."
-> hub

=== orbius
~ set naevius_orbius
"Orbius?" Naevius sobers. "An honest man, poor fellow. Twenty-five years in the Seventh, and they gave him a depot instead of a farm because he can count. He drinks alone and he coughs and he teaches the hostage children their letters himself, because the army won't pay a teacher." He shakes his head. "He'll die of that cough. Or of honesty. Whichever is quicker in a war."
-> hub
